# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repo AND in the working tree.
#
# Not cosmetic. Git on Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, so without
# this a fresh clone here checks out CRLF — and then:
#
#   - `pnpm format:check` fails on every file, because .prettierrc pins
#     `endOfLine: lf`;
#   - every drift gate (tokens:check, icons:check, fonts:check, api:check)
#     fails, because the generators write LF and the checked-out file is CRLF.
#
# It has not bitten yet only because every file in this repo was authored on
# this machine and has never been through a checkout conversion. The first
# clone would have hit all of it at once.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never inspects or converts them.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
